# UI Architecture

Hybrid pattern: UI listens to domain events; input opens windows via a narrow facade. Static `UserInterface` is Toolkit plumbing only.

## Rules

1. **UI listens to the game.** Controllers subscribe to domain events (`NetworkClient`, `Playfield`, stats). Gameplay raises facts; UI decides presentation.
2. **One feature = Controller + View + UXML/USS.** Controller owns flow and domain deps. View owns `VisualElement` queries and clicks. No networking in views; no Toolkit in game systems.
3. **`UserInterface` is Toolkit plumbing only.** Static load/style/panel helpers. Never add game APIs (`ToggleInventory`, `SetHealth`). Do not inject or register it in Reflex.
4. **Open/toggle via narrow facade (`IGameHud`).** Input may call `Open`/`Close`/`Toggle(WindowId)`. Do not inject Views or a fat UI hub into gameplay.
5. **Dependencies flow UI → Game.** Thin high-level exceptions OK (`LoadingScreen.Show`/`HideFade`). Never inject Views into combat/network/playfield.
6. **Prefer existing domain C# events** over a new global message bus.
7. **`IUINotifyService` is input gating only** (pointer over UI / drag), not a general UI API.
8. **World overlay (nameplates/hits) stays reactive** and separate from the window shell — do not route every HUD pixel through `IGameHud`.

## Patterns

```csharp
// ✅ Reactive: UI controller subscribes to domain
_networkClient.AttackInfoReceived += OnAttackInfo;

// ✅ Intentional: input toggles via facade
_gameHud.Toggle(WindowId.Character);

// ✅ View loads Toolkit via static helper
_menu = UserInterface.Load(this, "UI/Inventory", sortOrder: 80);

// ❌ Fat hub / game APIs on UserInterface
UserInterface.Instance.ToggleCharacterPanel();
UserInterface.SetHealth(hp);

// ❌ Game systems depending on Views
containerBuilder.RegisterValue(inventoryView);
```
